Day 29: Light in the Darkness | Wednesday of the Fourth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“I am the light of the world.”
A promise that reaches into every shadowed place of your heart.

Welcome to Day 29 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you to step into the gentle, steady light of Christ — a light that does not shame you, but guides you; a light that does not expose to embarrass, but reveals to heal; a light that remains faithful even when everything else feels uncertain.

This spoken‑word devotional meets you in the places that feel dim, confusing, or heavy. Jesus does not ask you to run toward the light — He simply asks you to take one step. No darkness is too deep for His love to reach.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Christ’s light is gentle, patient, and steady

How Jesus meets you in the places that feel uncertain

Why darkness is never the end of the story

A prayer to let His light guide your steps

A simple daily activity: lighting a candle and whispering, “Jesus, shine Your light here.”

